{"title":"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many positive two-digit whole numbers are divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/7/487bc4e5ed2785c243bc6f788ba6497c521a7165.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 11 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 9 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 15 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 12 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"387\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can simply list all of the numbers and then count how many there are. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is too small and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/1/791f15f656db201fa9116a2f762a4b292fc50883.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$105$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> is too large. We have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/8/018505a1ff9781a8493d5d41549494280be6adc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14, 21, 28, 35, 42, 49, 56, 63, 70, 77, 84, 91, 98$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"335\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>We see that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/0/0a08e2afabf7f76aa1dcc862a79f136cfa0da293.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(E) } 13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" /> numbers in the list.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/2/202bcba699e42aa9633c69d750c286b2f5064f30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14 = 2 \\times 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/8/8f8c562cc1940b7559026ab7b1690d4ca84ed332.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$98 = 14 \\times 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> are the smallest and largest numbers possible, respectively.\n</p><p>Thus, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/4/c54b149bfa347f269f0f3ff94048c50db6ee1a65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14 - 2 + 1 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(E) } 13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"170\" height=\"30\" /> positive two-digit multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/